From 6e945719da315a99f95f1c521c0f146d774cc6c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dquillman <davequillman@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 20:58:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] perf/sec: shrink the logo, add security headers, publish
 llms.txt
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Acting on the real PageSpeed run (desktop, Sep 5): performance 61,
best practices 77, agentic browsing 1/3. My earlier local Lighthouse numbers
were unusable for performance — the sandbox's observed first paint was 13s, so
its Speed Index measured the container, not the site. These three changes come
from the real report.

1. The logo was a 158 KB image rendered at 32 px

   public/favicon.png is 500x500 and 158 KB, and every <img> on the site pointed
   at it — the nav mark at 32 px, the footer at 24 px, the login card at 48 px.
   That is essentially all of PSI's "improve image delivery, est. savings
   166 KiB", and it was on the critical path of every page.

   Added logo-64.png (6.6 KB) and logo-128.png (19 KB) and pointed the rendered
   <img> tags at them: 158 KB -> 6.6 KB for the nav and footer marks, a 96%
   reduction. favicon.png stays exactly as it is — it is still the <link
   rel="icon"> and the Organization JSON-LD logo, where 500x500 is correct.

2. Security headers

   PSI's Trust and Safety section was four of the five best-practices failures.
   Fixed the two that can be fixed without risk, in firebase.json:

   - Strict-Transport-Security was max-age=31556926 with no includeSubDomains,
     which is why "use a strong HSTS policy" failed. Now
     max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload.
   - Clickjacking: X-Frame-Options: DENY for older agents plus a
     Content-Security-Policy of frame-ancestors 'none' for modern ones.
   - Also added X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff and a Referrer-Policy.

   Deliberately NOT fixed: "ensure CSP is effective against XSS" and "mitigate
   DOM-based XSS with Trusted Types" will still fail. A real content policy has
   to enumerate every origin the app talks to — Firebase, GA4, Meta, Clarity,
   Fontshare — and one omission takes the site down. Trusted Types would require
   reworking every innerHTML path. Both are worth doing deliberately, with a
   Report-Only rollout, not bundled into an image-size commit. So expect best
   practices to improve but not reach 100.

   X-Frame-Options: DENY means nothing can embed cipherexam.com in an iframe.
   Firebase Auth's own iframes live on the auth domain, not here, so popup and
   redirect sign-in are unaffected — but if anything is deliberately embedding
   the site, this is the change that would break it.

3. llms.txt

   PSI's new Agentic Browsing category scored 1/3, one failure being a missing
   llms.txt. Added one describing the product, the Bloom's-level method, the
   exam coverage and honest pricing, with all 23 indexable URLs grouped by
   purpose. Every link in it is verified present in sitemap.xml.

Verified: tsc -b clean, vite build clean, prerender 23/23, 99 tests pass,
Lighthouse accessibility 100 with zero failures.

